1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:25,280
 [music]

2
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:27,360
 Well, good morning, Watermark! How are we doing today?

3
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,200
 [applause]

4
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,400
 All right. Hey, good to see you. I'm so glad you made it.

5
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:38,560
 If this is your first time with us on a Sunday morning, let me just say welcome.

6
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:44,960
 And my hope for you today is you would take either your first or your next step with Jesus Christ.

7
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:50,080
 It's an extra special morning because many of you are here for Awaken.

8
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:52,160
 If you're here for Awaken, would you just let us know?

9
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:56,560
 [applause]

10
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:59,600
 So if you're here for Awaken, let me just welcome you to church.

11
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,400
 Welcome to Watermark Community Church.

12
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:09,840
 And if you are here for church because you call Watermark home, let me welcome you to Awaken.

13
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:15,360
 We're glad that we all get to be together today to worship the Lord.

14
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:19,040
 If you're here for Awaken, here's my hope.

15
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:24,320
 My hope for you is that just by joining us for church this Sunday morning,

16
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:29,440
 I hope that you would be reminded that Jesus did come to save you from sin,

17
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:34,880
 but he also came to save you into a family with brothers and sisters in the faith.

18
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:39,440
 And the Christian life was never made--you were never made to live it alone.

19
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:44,560
 And so if you live here in Dallas and you don't have a church family that you belong to,

20
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:46,240
 come join us here at Watermark.

21
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:52,080
 If you don't live in Dallas, then go home and find a church family to plug into.

22
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:57,440
 I'm really excited because this morning you're going to get to hear from David Platt.

23
00:01:57,440 --> 00:02:01,280
 And if you're not familiar with David, David,

24
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:07,040
 he is the lead pastor of McLean Bible Church in the Washington, D.C. area.

25
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:08,720
 He's an author.

26
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:15,920
 He's the founder and leader of Radical, a ministry that exists to take Jesus everywhere,

27
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:17,600
 to the end of the earth.

28
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:22,560
 And I've known David for several years, and here's what I would say about him.

29
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:24,720
 He is the real deal.

30
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:28,240
 There are people that when I get around them,

31
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:35,520
 I find myself just unbelievably encouraged by their genuine faith in the Lord.

32
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:39,680
 And I can honestly say that in the times that I get to be around David,

33
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:45,520
 I always leave wanting to enjoy greater intimacy with the Lord.

34
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:48,400
 And I believe you're going to experience that this morning.

35
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:56,960
 I also just want you to know that God used David's voice in my life back in 2019 to help

36
00:02:56,960 --> 00:03:04,160
 open my eyes to the responsibility that I have in taking the gospel to the end of the earth,

37
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:05,040
 to the nations.

38
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:10,480
 Like I have a part to play in the Great Commission, making disciples of all nations.

39
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:15,280
 And so if Watermark is your church home, you've heard me talk about how we are a

40
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:19,920
 sending church, that we feel responsibility for the gospel to go.

41
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:26,160
 And we celebrate people who leave Dallas and go to the end of the earth with the gospel.

42
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:32,960
 God used David's voice as a shaping voice in my life in helping me understand that.

43
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:41,120
 The last thing I'd say before I bring David up is if you're here and you love the Tubbs,

44
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:47,200
 you know I got those from David Platt.

45
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:52,720
 So if you were here last Sunday and you saw the Tubbs, I got those from David.

46
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:55,600
 So if you love the Tubbs, you love David Platt.

47
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:59,280
 So would you do an incredible job of welcoming David Platt to the stage today?

48
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:11,200
 And I want us to just take a moment and pray just like we do every Sunday morning.

49
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:17,200
 And if you're not normally here with us, we really believe that when we open up the Bible,

50
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:21,360
 the Word of God, it's like we're opening God's mouth and we can hear from him.

51
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:23,920
 He wants to speak to you today.

52
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:28,080
 So I want to invite you right now to pray for yourself and say, "God,

53
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:31,040
 allow me to hear from you today.

54
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:32,960
 Speak to my heart."

55
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:41,680
 And then would you pray for the people around you and ask God to speak to them as well?

56
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:53,280
 And then would you pray for David and ask God to speak through him to you?

57
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:09,120
 Well, Lord, I thank you in advance for what you have in store for this time that we have together.

58
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:14,240
 And I want to just ask and pray.

59
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:15,840
 You are here, God.

60
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,280
 We know that.

61
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,080
 We believe that.

62
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:22,400
 But I pray that you would make yourself overwhelmingly evident to us.

63
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:29,120
 Holy Spirit, I'm asking for your supernatural work in every single person's heart

64
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,320
 in the room this morning.

65
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:35,040
 I pray that you would illuminate our hearts and our minds to the truth.

66
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:40,800
 Would you give us the ability to see Christ clearly so that he would be fully glorified

67
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,640
 in our lives, Lord God?

68
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:48,880
 If there's anyone here today who does not know you, does not have saving faith,

69
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:52,880
 I pray that right now would be the moment of salvation for them.

70
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:56,560
 Would you call us to yourself and may we respond?

71
00:05:56,560 --> 00:06:01,200
 And I pray that you would strengthen David, that you would fill him full,

72
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:03,920
 and that you would minister to us through him.

73
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:04,800
 We love you, Lord.

74
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:05,840
 We give this time to you.

75
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:07,040
 In Jesus' name we pray.

76
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,340
 Amen.

77
00:06:08,340 --> 00:06:09,300
 Amen.

78
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:16,640
 Well, if you have a Bible, and I hope you or somebody around you does,

79
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:21,040
 that you can look on with, let me invite you to open with me to Mark chapter 11.

80
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:28,720
 Feel free to use table of contents if you need to, it's in the latter part of the Bible.

81
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,800
 Mark chapter 11.

82
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:39,280
 And while you're turning there, I want to say a few things before we hear from God in his word.

83
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:45,840
 One, I thank God for your pastor, T.A.

84
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:50,480
 Ever since the first moment I met him years ago,

85
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:58,080
 I was just immediately struck by what I believe is the humility

86
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:08,720
 and meekness and gentleness and boldness and compassion and courage

87
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:12,800
 that can only come from Jesus in him.

88
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:17,040
 And I trust those of you who are part of this Watermark family know

89
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:22,800
 the favor God has given you in being shepherded by him.

90
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:28,080
 And I just want to thank God publicly for his friendship to me and his example to me.

91
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:37,360
 Second, I want to thank God for the fruit of this church far beyond this church,

92
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:39,040
 including in my church family.

93
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:43,440
 So there are countless couples in Metro Washington, D.C.

94
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:51,280
 who have experienced restoration from brokenness through re-engage and countless

95
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:57,920
 individuals who've experienced complete transformation through regen.

96
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:03,360
 And that's the fruit of God's grace in this place, resounding far beyond this place.

97
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:10,080
 Which leads to number three, I thank God for Kylan and this entire porch team for leading.

98
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:16,000
 Yeah, give it up, especially Awakened, but a ministry to young adults here

99
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,520
 that goes far beyond here.

100
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:21,680
 And I'm honored to be a part of this conference this weekend.

101
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:28,320
 And I am just so thankful for him and for his team's commitment to pray

102
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:35,920
 and to prepare a conference with longing for an outpouring of God's spirit,

103
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:39,520
 not just to go through the motions of a conference.

104
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:43,840
 G. Campbell Morgan said, "We cannot organize revival,

105
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:47,440
 but we can set our sails to catch the wind from heaven

106
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:50,480
 when God chooses to blow upon his people once again."

107
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:54,400
 And I believe the sails are set this morning.

108
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:57,920
 Which leads to the fourth thing I want to share.

109
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:02,080
 I want to let you know where the next few minutes are headed,

110
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:08,080
 because this sermon is definitely not the main event in this service.

111
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:11,760
 The main event is coming a few minutes from now,

112
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:17,680
 when each one of you is going to have an opportunity to respond

113
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:28,640
 to an invitation from God to seek him with all your heart in this room.

114
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:33,680
 And I'm confident that every person within the sound of my voice

115
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:38,000
 needs to seek God in this room today.

116
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:43,520
 Some of you need to seek God for salvation in your life.

117
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:50,560
 Some of you need to seek God through honest confession of sin.

118
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:55,840
 Some of you need to seek God for help, for guidance,

119
00:09:55,840 --> 00:10:02,720
 for healing physically, emotionally, relationally, spiritually.

120
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:06,880
 And some of you need to seek God for others.

121
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:11,360
 I'm 100% confident that everybody in this gathering

122
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:17,040
 desperately needs to cry out in some way to God today.

123
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:21,360
 But not all of you will choose to do so.

124
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:26,720
 So a few moments from now, this room will divide into two groups,

125
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:29,680
 participants and observers.

126
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:35,040
 One group will seek God passionately,

127
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:40,880
 and the other group will observe others passively.

128
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:45,840
 And these are really the only two possible options.

129
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:50,000
 Some of you will choose to seek God passionately

130
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,680
 by calling out to him in praise and thanksgiving

131
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:58,080
 and confession and repentance and intercession and petition.

132
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:02,880
 While others of you will choose to observe,

133
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:06,720
 you'll watch people around you seeking God,

134
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:11,360
 but you won't seek God yourself for any number of reasons.

135
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:14,000
 Some of you will be afraid of what others might think of you.

136
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,080
 If you start crying out to God,

137
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:24,160
 some of you will be uncomfortable to leave a box you feel really comfortable in.

138
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:31,920
 Some of you will be afraid of what might happen if you truly seek and worship God.

139
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:34,560
 In your life.

140
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:39,200
 And some of you will say to yourself, maybe I'll seek God later.

141
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,480
 I'm just not ready right now.

142
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:43,440
 So I could go on and on, but for a variety of reasons,

143
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:46,800
 some of you will choose to observe rather than participate.

144
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:53,680
 And to be clear, please note what is not an option, seeking God casually.

145
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:57,280
 Because that is impossible.

146
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:05,760
 When you truly encounter God, you either bow and worship or turn and run.

147
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:10,080
 So before we go any further, I know we just prayed,

148
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:13,840
 but now that you know where all this is headed,

149
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:18,640
 I want to pray not just that we would be able to hear,

150
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:27,200
 but that we would have courage, grace, God's help to respond.

151
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,320
 So would you bow your heads with me just one more time?

152
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:40,080
 Oh, God.

153
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:49,280
 Help us.

154
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:55,200
 To feel the weight and the wonder.

155
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:02,080
 Of what we're doing even right now.

156
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:16,320
 Talking to you and asking you to speak to us.

157
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:21,520
 So yes, we pray, please.

158
00:13:21,520 --> 00:13:25,280
 We need spiritual eyes to see, ears to hear.

159
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:30,000
 We won't be able to hear you speak without your spirit's help.

160
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:37,920
 And we won't be able to respond and experience you

161
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:43,120
 in all the ways you want us to without your help.

162
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:53,760
 Only you can produce authentic, passionate, wholehearted, honest,

163
00:13:54,880 --> 00:14:03,040
 humble, seriously joyful, spirit-directed, Jesus-centered worship.

164
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:09,520
 So we pray that you would do it by your power, by your spirit in the next few minutes

165
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:17,840
 in ways that can only be explained by your hand and only be attributed to your glory.

166
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:22,000
 God, we pray for this.

167
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,960
 We ask for this in Jesus' name.

168
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:28,800
 If you agree with that prayer, would you say amen?

169
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:33,440
 Okay, here we go.

170
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,960
 Mark chapter 11.

171
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:37,920
 So I'm going to get us there.

172
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:43,600
 In the first gathering this morning, I preached from a different text of scripture, Isaiah 55.

173
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:51,280
 I'm going to put it on the screen because it sets the stage for what we're about to look at

174
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:52,400
 in Mark 11.

175
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:57,360
 So Isaiah 55, 6 says, "Seek the Lord while he may be found.

176
00:14:57,360 --> 00:15:00,160
 Call upon him while he is near."

177
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:04,880
 This is an invitation from God to seek him.

178
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:12,720
 So this is coming straight from God to us, and he's saying, "I'm near to you."

179
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:18,720
 And this is where I want to take this to a whole other level.

180
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:25,520
 If some of you stayed around from the first gathering, because God is not just near to us

181
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:26,800
 in a vague sense.

182
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:36,400
 God, for those who know him and are in relationship with him, is actually in us.

183
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:46,720
 First Corinthians 6, 19 says, "Christian, do not know your body is a temple of the

184
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:50,240
 Holy Spirit within you, whom you have from God."

185
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,040
 That's nearness.

186
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:56,640
 If you're a follower of Jesus, you have the Holy Spirit.

187
00:15:56,640 --> 00:16:00,960
 God, a trinity, Father, Son, Holy Spirit.

188
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:05,600
 You have God, the Holy Spirit, living inside you.

189
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:08,160
 Cue the tubs.

190
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:13,920
 So that's nearness, living inside your body.

191
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,960
 God, that's amazing nearness.

192
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:18,960
 You can't get any nearer than that.

193
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:21,920
 And not just individually.

194
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:24,160
 So listen to First Corinthians 3, 16, and 17.

195
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:29,360
 "Do not know that you are God's temple, and that God's Spirit dwells in you.

196
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:32,240
 If anyone destroys God's temple, God will destroy him.

197
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:34,720
 For God's temple is holy, and you are that temple."

198
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:39,360
 Now, initially, it looks like this is saying the same thing as First Corinthians 6, but

199
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:43,120
 it's not, because the "you" here is plural.

200
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:46,800
 So these verses are actually talking about the church.

201
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:54,240
 The gathering of God's people is where God's Spirit dwells.

202
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:59,360
 God's temple is the gathering of God's people.

203
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:04,880
 So both pictures, individually and together.

204
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:08,640
 God's temple, Spirit, dwelling in us.

205
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:16,240
 So keep that in mind as we now read Mark 11, verse 12 and following.

206
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:21,920
 "And the following day, when they came from Bethany, Jesus was hungry, and seeing in the

207
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:24,960
 distance a fig tree and leaf, he went to see if he could find anything on it.

208
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:29,040
 When he came to it, he found nothing but leaves, for it was not the season for figs.

209
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:34,240
 And he said to it, 'May no one ever eat fruit from you again.'

210
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:36,160
 And his disciples heard it.

211
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:43,920
 And they came to Jerusalem, and he entered the temple and began to drive out those who

212
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,920
 sold and those who bought in the temple.

213
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:52,320
 And he overturned the tables of the moneychangers and the seats of those who sold pigeons, and

214
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:55,280
 he would not allow anyone to carry anything through the temple.

215
00:17:55,280 --> 00:18:02,080
 And he was teaching them and saying to them, 'Is it not written, "My house shall be

216
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:07,200
 called a house of prayer for all the nations, but you have made it a den of robbers."'"

217
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:11,520
 "And the chief priests and the scribes heard it and were seeking a way to destroy him,

218
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:14,880
 for they feared him, because all the crowd was astonished at his teaching.

219
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:17,680
 When evening came, they went out of the city.

220
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:22,240
 As they passed by in the morning, they saw the fig tree withered away to its roots.

221
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:27,200
 And Peter remembered and said to him, 'Rabbi, look, the fig tree that you cursed is withered.'

222
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:30,560
 And Jesus answered them, 'Have faith in God.

223
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:35,680
 Truly I say to you, whoever says to this mountain, "Be taken up and thrown into the

224
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:40,560
 sea," and does not doubt in his heart, but believes that what he says will come to pass,

225
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:41,680
 it will be done for him.

226
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:46,320
 Therefore I tell you, whatever you ask in prayer, believe that you have received it,

227
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:47,360
 and it will be yours.

228
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:50,480
 Whenever you stand praying, forgive.

229
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:56,160
 If you have anything against anyone, so that your Father also, who is in heaven, may forgive

230
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:57,200
 your trespasses."'"

231
00:18:57,200 --> 00:19:02,960
 So the way Mark tells this story is really important.

232
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:08,560
 So the setting is the week where Jesus is about to die on the cross.

233
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:14,240
 That Sunday, he had entered the city, which was packed with people for the Passover feast.

234
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,920
 He looked around, and then he left.

235
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:22,240
 And then the Bible says, "The following day," so we're on Monday now, Jesus is walking back

236
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:23,280
 toward the city.

237
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:28,480
 Jesus speaks to this fig tree that doesn't have any fruit, and he curses it.

238
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:35,920
 Then his disciples go into Jerusalem, he overturns these tables in the temple.

239
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:43,040
 Then he leaves, and on the following day, the next morning, they're walking back toward

240
00:19:43,040 --> 00:19:43,760
 the city.

241
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:48,480
 Jesus sees this fig tree, the disciples see it, and it's withered.

242
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:59,360
 And Mark intentionally sandwiches this story of the cleansing of the temple in between

243
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:02,480
 this cursing of a fig tree to make a point.

244
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:08,080
 Because throughout the Old Testament, God had often compared his people, Israel, to

245
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:08,800
 a fig tree.

246
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:15,360
 Places like Jeremiah 8, Joel chapter 1, where God described how Israel's religion was dead

247
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:18,480
 and fruitless because they were unfaithful to him.

248
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:25,520
 So now, this picture of a fig tree with no fruit in Mark becomes a picture of the religion

249
00:20:25,520 --> 00:20:28,800
 that's being practiced at the temple in Jerusalem.

250
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:33,360
 Now, on the outside, it looked like everything was thriving.

251
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:35,040
 Think about it.

252
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:39,600
 They had people, multitudes, crowds of them coming to celebrate the Passover.

253
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:41,680
 They had the word of God.

254
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:48,080
 In addition to all kinds of other laws they'd worked hard to keep, they had worship every

255
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,240
 day in the temple with all kinds of sacrifices.

256
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:55,920
 They had offerings they would bring and give, feasts they would observe.

257
00:20:55,920 --> 00:21:01,920
 They had an abundance of religious activity, but they were totally missing the point.

258
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:11,840
 They had all the trappings of religion, crowds, God's word, God's worship, offerings, all

259
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:16,960
 kinds of activity, but they were completely missing God.

260
00:21:19,120 --> 00:21:26,640
 And today, I want to ask the question, is it possible for us to do the same thing?

261
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:32,560
 Realizing we don't go to a temple today.

262
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:34,720
 This building at Watermark is not a temple.

263
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:37,280
 We just read 1 Corinthians 3 and 6.

264
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:40,160
 We are the temple, individually and together.

265
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:51,200
 So is it possible for us to carry on the trappings of religion, crowds of people, the word of

266
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:59,920
 God, the worship of God, songs, offerings, all kinds of religious activity, to do all

267
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:03,120
 of that and actually miss God?

268
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:12,320
 And I think it's not just possible, particularly across the American South.

269
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:14,080
 I think it's probable.

270
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:22,880
 If I were to give a title to this message today, it would be "The Curse of Cultural

271
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:32,560
 Christianity," because we have subtly and in many ways unknowingly become accustomed

272
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:39,840
 today to a form of Christianity that Jesus desires to completely overthrow.

273
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:53,680
 Let me show you what they were missing in the temple that we are prone to miss as the

274
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:54,180
 temple.

275
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:57,040
 At least four things they were missing.

276
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:07,040
 One, reverent, fearful, awe-filled worship.

277
00:23:07,040 --> 00:23:15,920
 Reverent, fearful, awe-filled worship.

278
00:23:15,920 --> 00:23:23,200
 All these people were doing all this activity supposedly in the worship of God, but they

279
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:29,280
 were missing reverence, fear, awe of the God they were worshiping.

280
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:33,680
 This was, think about it, holy ground they were on.

281
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:38,560
 The temple was the place where the glory of God dwelled among his people.

282
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:47,520
 Remember the scene from 2 Chronicles chapter 7, when Solomon originally dedicated the

283
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,240
 temple?

284
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:51,440
 As soon as Solomon finished his prayer, what happened?

285
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:55,680
 Fire came down from heaven, consumed the burnt offerings and the sacrifices.

286
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:58,720
 The glory of the Lord filled the temple.

287
00:23:58,720 --> 00:24:03,760
 The priests could not enter the house of the Lord because the glory of the Lord filled

288
00:24:03,760 --> 00:24:04,560
 the Lord's house.

289
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:09,760
 When all the people of Israel saw the fire come down and the glory of the Lord on the

290
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:14,400
 temple, they bowed down with their faces to the ground on the pavement, and they worshiped

291
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:19,520
 and gave thanks to the Lord, saying, "For he is good, for his steadfast love endures

292
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:20,020
 forever."

293
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:23,600
 That's what you do in the temple.

294
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:32,320
 You bow down with your face on the ground, on the pavement, and you worship and you give

295
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:32,820
 thanks.

296
00:24:32,820 --> 00:24:41,440
 This is the place where 750 years before, Isaiah wrote, "I saw the Lord sitting upon

297
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:43,600
 a throne, high and lifted up.

298
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:45,680
 The train of his rope filled the temple.

299
00:24:45,680 --> 00:24:48,000
 Above him stood the seraphim.

300
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:51,680
 Each had these angels, six wings, with two he covered his face, with two he covered his

301
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:52,960
 feet, with two he flew.

302
00:24:52,960 --> 00:24:57,360
 And one called to another and said, 'Holy, holy, holy is the Lord of hosts.

303
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:59,280
 The whole earth is full of his glory.'

304
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:05,760
 And the foundations, the threshold shook at the voice of him who called, and the house

305
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:06,640
 was filled with smoke."

306
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:14,960
 And now, fast forward centuries, there's none of this awe.

307
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:18,480
 Nobody's on their face.

308
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:22,080
 Nobody's in holy fear, trembling.

309
00:25:22,080 --> 00:25:25,840
 Did you notice verse 16 in Mark 11?

310
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:29,360
 Jesus would not allow anyone to carry anything through the temple.

311
00:25:29,360 --> 00:25:31,760
 People were using the temple as a pass-through.

312
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:34,160
 You want to get from one side of the city to the other?

313
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:35,600
 It's too long to walk around.

314
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:36,720
 Just walk through it.

315
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:37,920
 Save some time.

316
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:43,040
 So you have all these people just casually walking through the temple with no thought

317
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:44,400
 of the glory of God.

318
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:46,960
 No awe of the majesty of God.

319
00:25:46,960 --> 00:25:49,360
 No fear of the holiness of God.

320
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:54,720
 Now you think about what Isaiah said after his vision of God in the temple.

321
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:56,560
 I said, "Woe is me.

322
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:57,200
 I am lost.

323
00:25:57,200 --> 00:25:58,160
 I am a man of unclean lips.

324
00:25:58,160 --> 00:25:59,840
 I dwell in the midst of a people of unclean lips.

325
00:25:59,840 --> 00:26:02,480
 My eyes have seen the King, the Lord of hosts."

326
00:26:02,480 --> 00:26:08,160
 Isaiah was undone in the presence of the Holy King and Lord of heavenly armies.

327
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:09,920
 Ezra, same way, Ezra 10, 1.

328
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:15,600
 "While Ezra prayed and made confession, weeping and casting himself down before the house

329
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:19,200
 of God, the temple, a very great assembly of men, women, and children gathered him out

330
00:26:19,200 --> 00:26:19,760
 of Israel.

331
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:22,160
 For the people wept bitterly."

332
00:26:22,160 --> 00:26:24,560
 Imagine this scene at the temple.

333
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:31,280
 People making confession, weeping, casting themselves down before the house of God in

334
00:26:31,280 --> 00:26:32,800
 contrition over sin.

335
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:36,000
 So here's the question.

336
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:40,880
 Is it possible for us to come into a gathering like this, as the temple?

337
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:47,120
 We are the dwelling place of the glory of the same God right now.

338
00:26:47,120 --> 00:26:52,720
 Is it possible for us to come in here, sing songs, say prayers, open the Bible without

339
00:26:52,720 --> 00:27:03,360
 fear, without reverence, without awe, before God?

340
00:27:05,280 --> 00:27:14,400
 If we really realize we're the dwelling place, the presence of the God who's holy,

341
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:20,720
 holy, holy before whom angels cover their face and people fall on their faces, wouldn't

342
00:27:20,720 --> 00:27:23,760
 it make sense at some point that we would be right here?

343
00:27:31,040 --> 00:27:40,000
 Not just at some point, wouldn't we spend a lot of time right here?

344
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:50,080
 Why is this such a rare posture in our worship?

345
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:54,000
 Why would that be like an unusual thing?

346
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,960
 Oh, there are people on their faces before God.

347
00:27:56,960 --> 00:27:58,880
 I had never seen it.

348
00:28:01,760 --> 00:28:02,720
 It's the same God.

349
00:28:02,720 --> 00:28:10,240
 We've just gotten accustomed to coming and sitting, and I don't just say this because

350
00:28:10,240 --> 00:28:10,720
 of this building.

351
00:28:10,720 --> 00:28:16,880
 It's the same in the building where I pastor, in theater-style seats to watch a stage, to

352
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:24,720
 observe, like we do in front of a million other screens in the world.

353
00:28:27,360 --> 00:28:34,000
 And meanwhile, I wonder if all of heaven is just shouting, "Do you realize who you're

354
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:34,720
 talking to?

355
00:28:34,720 --> 00:28:41,440
 Do you realize who you're singing to?

356
00:28:41,440 --> 00:28:44,080
 Do you realize what you're doing?"

357
00:28:44,080 --> 00:28:54,800
 And we might say, "Well, I mean, I can't see myself getting down on my face.

358
00:28:56,160 --> 00:29:02,000
 What would people think?" Or maybe you just, "I don't want them to think I'm, like,

359
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:02,960
 super spiritual."

360
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:05,040
 Why are you even thinking about what other people think?

361
00:29:05,040 --> 00:29:06,320
 You're in the presence of God.

362
00:29:06,320 --> 00:29:08,880
 Get your eyes off yourself.

363
00:29:08,880 --> 00:29:09,360
 Totally.

364
00:29:09,360 --> 00:29:14,000
 Isaiah's not like, "Huh, what are people going to think about me?"

365
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:20,880
 Ezra, "No, he's just weeping before God because he's in awe of God."

366
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:31,360
 That's what I mean by reverent, awe-filled, fearful worship of God.

367
00:29:31,360 --> 00:29:42,000
 And I would add this posture, not just in our gathering, but is this posture regular

368
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:42,800
 in your life?

369
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:43,920
 Remember, you're the temple.

370
00:29:43,920 --> 00:29:48,880
 Like, is this a daily place for you?

371
00:29:53,120 --> 00:29:56,640
 And if not, at least ask the question, "Why not?"

372
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:59,520
 You're the temple of the living God.

373
00:29:59,520 --> 00:30:07,120
 Why is it not a regular practice to be on your face before him in just awe of who he

374
00:30:07,120 --> 00:30:07,620
 is?

375
00:30:07,620 --> 00:30:12,240
 So you see, they were missing God.

376
00:30:12,240 --> 00:30:15,440
 It's possible for us to miss God.

377
00:30:15,440 --> 00:30:20,160
 So that's the first thing they were missing.

378
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:26,160
 Which leads to second thing, sorrowful confession of sin.

379
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:31,920
 Sorrowful confession of sin, which is obviously happening here in Ezra 10.

380
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:34,720
 Weeping on their faces.

